    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In issue 1927, a reporter using provider v1.15.1 and Terraform v1.5.7 confirmed that using `threshold_config` instead of `metric_threshold_config` solved the billing-alert configuration problem. Maintainer oarbusi explained that `metric_threshold_config` requires `metric_name` and advised `threshold_config` instead. The resource documentation requires `metric_threshold_config` when `event_type` is `OUTSIDE_METRIC_THRESHOLD` or `OUTSIDE_SERVERLESS_METRIC_THRESHOLD`. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/issues/1927",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3242b64c3844d473a9a3af23f150d63c29fabcaa717043d459b730f074fd7b3a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
