    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Terraform and Pulumi document importing an existing alert configuration with the composite identifier project_id-alert_configuration_id; their examples use terraform import and pulumi import respectively. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://registry.terraform.io/providers/mongodb/mongodbatlas/latest/docs/resources/alert_configuration",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:63ec7bf1ec1da8d98716294e6d96fc2fba1352671ed1fd2bc79380d921137e86",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:058a77c83b30e2951dbcd8e241cacf6b0087da30bd794595131fd1636c8a1fe6",
            "ev:45956f25357f50a6db837cb448ea027d2c198de1305386304ccf6c3f20feb304",
            "ev:8ec05e5b87d346e2c9cfaf4ccd191465ad60707d8f351c28d6bc9846efc730ac",
            "ev:e1b59d6a5fc57b025afb4a15e16b56ea334f1f18d854ad2031c25c76ade5f933"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.pulumi.com/registry/packages/mongodbatlas/api-docs/alertconfiguration/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Terraform alert resource documentation says some validations were removed to unblock alert creation as alert variables change, and directs readers to the Atlas API documentation for current information. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://registry.terraform.io/providers/mongodb/mongodbatlas/latest/docs/resources/alert_configuration",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1ee102d73a75536ecaa9f35f14afc4791e4cdf2d63098d545a27fb3a606926a7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:50962fb3710d4d7575b20e890c1ae435e74142607ec2a366422324f14a94316c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "HashiCorp documents that `terraform plan` and `terraform apply` refresh state against real infrastructure by default. A `-refresh-only` operation reviews and records drift without modifying remote infrastructure; normal plan or apply can instead attempt to revert manual changes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/tutorials/state/resource-drift",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1eadc9fe9c45d1b93fc7862c9cc269d8ea7256fd73728fd3542f050f375ba8b7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5ee6d6d73b456e3b4d18d230cf7ec7f2997488e7696a948e9a5818a5e77c7c94"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The reporter in issue 305 used Terraform v0.12.21 and Atlas provider 0.6.4. The report describes a billing alert deleted through the website causing a 404 during plan, and website changes to its event type or amount failing to be restored from configuration. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/issues/305",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2fb6cd4f0c585b7573907f8fa70aaf1a19c45a3c5e2cf6d4e3fcd65a9937f713",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:523788b5817d7336d99e8707359d937b024f2ad69f9fff0c7393a6c1551862cf"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The provider changelog lists a fix for alert-configuration drift detection in v1.8.1, dated March 7, 2023. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7352f6af47bd4ccde7223bef8d1b1c98ee44faae7ab5f6b3d75b35c444701900",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:dbdce332dddc617871fbb17196c3ad1d189ac341b2d6d6837cfcffa86f18b074"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The provider changelog lists avoiding a state difference after import for an undefined optional alert-notification attribute among the v1.12.0 changes, dated September 20, 2023. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b807940f0752850736e9bed16bf8be218604647e490ccd37931bbe6158845038",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:74290166b9ce51941b44cd7e47f5c0dd79cb003ae9532bcf697cd817ec3ade22"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Pulumi package states that it is based on the mongodbatlas Terraform Provider. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.pulumi.com/registry/packages/mongodbatlas/api-docs/alertconfiguration/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fac497a7abfd7d8610d8c6c10a0c9b2560e738bfec7a41a68c4f66d42be7503e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:189cac4095109c26e10ac7be559e3cd01483808d3518e327b4cdc3e0045e1ee4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the released Terraform provider v2.8.0 alert resource schema, `project_id` and `severity_override` each use `stringplanmodifier.RequiresReplace()`. The schema exposes the alert event, enablement, matchers, thresholds, and notifications separately. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/git/tags/e49de3204be1e2b47776c33e6b8833ae358f7de1",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c57411940b5bc19557afaefddbd2bf1d521f9c2520a1b91e9a9a1b35227f1e16",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5b9c7cf1cb185b4abe6fa2d0a0037900596345737ec232052d5f35e9ed3bee92",
            "ev:c6026c42796a2ec21688b77cd4e027e3c61e08fa341ffb6d9a3c73fed17483bb"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/v2.8.0/internal/service/alertconfiguration/resource.go"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In Terraform provider v2.20.1, the complete alert schema marks only `project_id` with `stringplanmodifier.RequiresReplace()`; `severity_override` is optional without that replacement modifier. The update method copies a changed severity value into the existing alert update request, and the read method still removes a missing resource from state. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://api.github.com/repos/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/git/tags/292c1b7006df191d5fca8b4aaa4e1cc87cc86d59",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7250696000f030162f84a0a1ffaf6768301833fc0f7ac2f9e39483f15aafeea7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
